  "worked_solution": "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bags. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of pounds.  \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in bag $A$,  we get\n\n$$\n13.30÷10=1.33\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $A$ is $$1.33$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in bag $B$,  we get\n\n$$\n11.20÷8=1.40\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$1.40$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in bag $C$,  we get\n\n$$\n9.00÷6=1.50\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $C$ is $$1.50$  per pound.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bag $A$ has the lowest unit price. Therefore, bag $A$ is the best deal.",
